doc An expression used as a statement.
  Lets an expression stand on its own line, which is how functions are
  called for their side effects, including functions that return nothing:

  ```
  fn shout()
    print "HEY"
  end

  shout()
  ```

  It is tried after every statement that starts with a keyword and after
  `assign`, so it never hides another statement form.

syntax statement
  {e: expr any}
